Aside from identifying bags of holding or cancelling monster, I have
found a number of uses for wand of cancellation -- can anyone add to
them?

1) Way to get a lot of water in a hurry. Don't want to risk the
fountain?  Don't have some way to walk on water so you can dip them in
a moat?  Simply drop all your potions in a corner and fire a cancel zap
at it. Presto -- more water than you know what to do with.

2)  Can also be named Wand of Mass Uncurse.
Example:  In a beginner move that shows I've been playing homeworld for
too long, I buy and wear an elven cloak which turns out to be -2
cursed.  I'm also wearing uncursed -1 low boots, because I haven't
found any other shoes.

Well, all my other armor is +0 uncursed, so after carefully divesting
myself of my other magic items, I shoot myself with the wand of
cancellation.  All my armor suddenly reverts to +0 uncursed, and that
means my AC drops by 4 points - 3 for resetting the wrong AC to 0, and
1 for the elven cloak's inherent protection.  So this collection of
useless junk is now fully
functional armor, and my ac is now 1 instead of 5.

Other uses? 

